@John S

In your Aussie pronunciation, do you believe you pronounce the -nce different from the -nts?  Or is it more a question of the A having a different sound?  (I suspect it's the latter.)

I'm anticipating that a lot of people will claim that the two words sound nothing alike, but unless you use a different A sound, you're probably pronouncing the consonant cluster the same in both words (in normal speech), all the while thinking you're not.

